use I saw real  miracles happen out on that ball field  and and even after that so uh it's I'm  lucky to be alive and it's just really  good to be with you I remember getting  an early report like a day two days  after and you had had a massive number  of blood transfusions and it was very  touch-and-go have doctors told you how  close you were to maybe not recovering  from this the  you know probably about a month after  when I was through all the surgeries I  asked my main trauma surgeon dr. Sava  said can you walk through with me what  really happened especially in those  first few days when I was unconscious I  didn't come to until about the fourth  day after I went to the hospital because  of all the surgeries and he said that  first day especially there were at least  two times where it could have gone the  other way and you know you look at look  at just getting to the hospital alive my  colleague from Ohio Brad Wenstrup if  he's not there a doctor a common Army  Ranger who who actually served combat  and helped get people to the hospital  from the battlefield he applied a  tourniquet that that slowed the bleeding  down and I would have bled out if I if I  didn't have that tourniquet applied  I don't what he wouldn't have even even  made what is your so what is your  recollection of the shooting  I remember hearing the first shot but  you're not thinking you were playing  baseball and you're not thinking there's  a there's a gunman shooting we're out on  a ball field I looked in a I saw a  tractor where the noise was coming from  and I figured maybe they detractor  backfired and then all of a sudden you  heard a few more shots and by that point  I got hit and went down and was hearing  a lot of gunfire back and forth that's  when my security detail  agents David Bailey they were amazing  engage the shooter they're truly always  there like they were there in an open  field with a pistol against a rifle and  yeah they were heavily outgunned but  look if they di